## Xiaomi proprietary component — never distributed

`miloco-mcp-server` loads a Xiaomi proprietary native library (shipped upstream
as `lib/libmiot_camera_lite.{dylib,so}`) for camera P2P streaming. That library
is proprietary to Xiaomi and is **never** downloaded, mirrored, bundled, or
redistributed by this plugin.

Some upstream builds do not include it. When it is absent, camera features are
unavailable while every other platform keeps working; the plugin reports that
condition explicitly (as a degraded state with a reason) instead of failing
silently or pretending the feature exists.

## Plugin dependencies

The plugin's own source pulls two normal npm libraries, declared in
`package.json` and installed by the package manager (they are not vendored or
re-published here):

| Package | License | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `qrcode` (with `pngjs`) | MIT | Renders the Tuya QR-login token as an image a phone can scan |
| `jsqr` | Apache-2.0 | **Development only** — decodes the generated image in the test suite, so a broken QR fails the build instead of the user |

